lines=['# vectorAdd: six-source F128/F256 negative control','', '**Finding:** F128 speeds up both CH and DH but CH improves more; F256 slows both, especially DH. DH F256 uses8.7030% more cycles than DH-P0 and5.9174% more cycles than matched CH. This occurs despite unchanged accepted read/miss/DRAM-read counts and much lower aggregate retry/admission events. It is a counterexample to using fewer retries as a sufficient predictor of faster performance.','', 'One frozen input, six closed accepted sources; both new CH results independently pass frozen read-only strict/true164/native-restore audits. No active scan/MVT result is read, no workload/configuration is dropped, and no per-program best variant is used for a GM. No model, source, registry, owner, controller, budget or paper was changed.','', '## Identity and real kernel contract','', 'Input digest `e7bb67e63e3c38478ff50db4dcc25dee9262fe195b30589547b1ac5e2bc3d799`. Canonical spec, full declared-body qualification, strict/raw statistics and bounded header agree: one stream0kernel `_Z6VecAddPKfS0_Pfi`,84,000,768active-thread instructions,23,438CTAs, grid(23438,1,1),block(256,1,1). This is the frozen DTC6M trace identity; the same-name EP4M input remains separate. No ATAX/BICG145m two-kernel shape is reused. Whole declared trace coverage does not newly prove capture-time ELF/numeric input or full native application identity.','', 'Fixed Core `9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70`, Framework `02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4`, binary SHA `02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d`. The four original references are exact original-index rows by full digest/cell/profile; the two new CH points keep STAGEII_AUTHORIZED_CH role. No R2/IR/EP/PQPS substitution or historical negative promotion occurs.','', '## Performance: all three profiles','',tab(['Profile','CH cycles','DH cycles','S_CH','S_DH','CH/DH','I=S_DH/S_CH'],[[p,by['CH',p]['cycles'],by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_CH']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p),1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_DH']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p),by['CH',p]['cycles']/by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['I']for x in d['matched_performance']if x['profile']==p)]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'F128 reduces CH cycles2.8532% and DH cycles1.9567%; I=0.990856 so the relative DTC advantage contracts. F256 increases CH cycles1.0041% and DH cycles8.7030%; I=0.929175 and DH now takes5.9174% more cycles than CH. All behavior is in the single captured kernel. This negative result remains part of the fixed input set.','', '## Fixed read traffic, changing writes and retry mix','', 'L2 GLOBAL read accepted/miss values use32-byte sectors; accepted excludes retries and misses=MISS+SECTOR_MISS. DRAM data values are issued32-byte atoms across20controllers. All six raw L2 access totals and all-L2 misses are2,250,000 with zero pending hits; GLOBAL read accepted/misses and issued DRAM reads are1,500,000. These units/populations remain distinct, even though some counts coincide here.','',tab(['Counter',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[label,*[by[c,p]['totals'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k,label in keys]),'', 'DH F256 vs P0: all-L2 retry events fall5,068,832 to2,472,990 (-51.21%), ICNT admission blocks fall4,943,384 to2,374,608 (-51.96%), yet cycles increase8.70%. DRAM writes rise633,008 to634,352 (+1,344atoms, about0.212%). Issued writes are measured during the replay, not proof of complete end-of-run dirty-cache drainage or a changed application store count. The small traffic change alone does not establish the cause of the much larger cycle regression.','']
