lines+=[tab(['Positive-only retry reason',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[k,*[by[c,p]['raw_reason_final_explicitly_printed'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k in reasonkeys]),'', 'DH read MISS_QUEUE_FULL falls4,980,069 ->4,142,175 ->311,125, while entry-capacity failures rise73,050 ->1,231,551 ->2,161,234. CH has the same qualitative substitution of fewer miss-queue retries and more entry-capacity failures. These are retry event counts, not occupancy or stall-cycle durations. MSHR entry capacity is distinct from an existing-address merge-list limit; unprinted merge reasons remain MISSING rather than inserted0. A lower sum of retries does not imply lower critical-path wait, and does not justify a capacity remedy by itself.','', '## Typed frontend and finite service','', 'CH PAPER_BASE common PIB256 and DH PAPER_OO PIB128 remain distinct. DH generic PIB8 is inactive for OO admission. CH common Tag/PIB counters are not OO fields; unprinted OO PIB-full/Tag-conflict counters stay null. Cross-design differences in L1/Tag/pool/queues/finite service/timing/area remain disclosed, so these are not equal-resource designs.','', 'All three DH runs explicitly print375,000OO new misses,0valid hits and0pending hits;375,000lower128B creations/issued/responses/acquired/released credits and1,500,000accepted read sectors conserve exactly. These explicit zeros are actual observations in the OO classification domain; they do not license filling missing fields with zero. The workload offers no observed OO read-line hit/merge benefit in this frozen replay. Static two-read/one-write source structure is not used as a substitute for these counters.','',tab(['DH profile','Mean PIB entries, all64SM samples','Mean physical lines','Ready-to-retire cycles / retired read entry','Map-loss-to-free cycles / event','Writeback wait events'],[[p,*[next(x for x in typed if x['cell']=='DH'and x['profile']==p)['DH_finite_service'][k]for k in['mean_PIB_entries_across_all64SMs','mean_physical_lines_across_all64SMs','fully_ready_to_retire_cycles_per_retired_entry','map_loss_to_free_cycles_per_recorded_event']],by['DH',p]['totals']['DTC_SERVICE_V1_wb_wait']]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'Finite-service retired denominator is375,000 read entries for each profile. F256 ready-to-complete sum844,101 exceeds P0 810,614 and F128 810,578; writeback wait40,069 exceeds26,947/26,012. Map-loss-to-free sum2,987,358 is much larger than191,409/343,023 for an equal342,232event denominator. These service-lifetime associations motivate examining tail/order behavior; their sums and per-entry ratios are not critical-path time or causal fractions. Means are sample/entry-specific; gauges/peaks are kept separate.','', '## Missing means and available extrema','', 'All six strict mean latency dictionaries are empty, while explicit DRAM reads are nonzero. Each single-kernel replay ends before500,000cycles; fixed print-before-stat-fold ordering can leave num_mfs0at printing and suppress mean lines. Missing mean latency therefore remains MISSING, never zero, and does not indicate failed integer parsing or no DRAM delay.','',tab(['Source','Printed max mflatency','Printed max MRQ','Printed max ICNT-to-memory','Printed max ICNT-to-shader'],[[c+'-'+p,*[next(x for x in lat if x['cell']==c and x['profile']==p)['raw_max_latency_diagnostics'].get(k)for k in['maxmflatency','maxmrqlatency','max_icnt2mem_latency','max_icnt2sh_latency']]]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'F256 has much larger printed maxima, especially DH mflatency46,970 versus P0 6,386/F128 4,741 and ICNT-to-memory44,545 versus5,827/4,402. These are extrema over their recorded event scope, not mean service time, exact queue residence or known critical loads. Their increase is a tail-behavior clue consistent with worsened ordering/response timing; it does not prove which request determined completion or isolate DRAM scheduling from shared credits, ICNT and finite service. No lifetime distribution or request-to-dependency map is available in these accepted logs.','', '## Configuration and evidence limits','', 'Within each design only FR-FCFS size64/128/256 changes, with coupled memory-partition shared-credit limits255/319/447 (return queue192, two subpartitions, private1each). DRAM850MHz and Core/ICNT/L2 clocks,10MiB L2 capacity/mapping and each design\'s frontend are fixed. F256 is not a pure isolated queue-capacity change and does not offer free/equal-area hardware.','', 'Atlas47a097aad4406893a07f8d230e1e0a850609bf39 maps the candidate source at CUDA application commitb059fdae25c2aabf737486aada743fca114469ce (`vectorAdd.cu:78-83;launch86-133`) to two coalesced FP32 read streams and one store, with no required cross-CTA reuse. FIXED_SOURCE_PHASE_MAPPING.json retains the exact prior source/report SHA references. Capture-time source/ELF/numeric binding remains unresolved; full-body qualification certifies this declared trace scope, not arbitrary CUDA Samples builds.','', 'Facts: matched F256 is negative despite unchanged reads/fewer visible retries, and certain printed service sums/extrema increase. Association: larger coupled window/credits changes timing and finite-service lifetimes. Hypothesis only: increased tail/ordering delays may outweigh reduced repeated admission attempts. Existing closed counters do not prove that mechanism or warrant a new experiment automatically. No new simulation or next48batch is scheduled.','', '## Reproduction and source locators','', 'Run `python3 analyze_three_profiles.py`, `python3 validate_vector_control.py`, `python3 render_vector_control.py` to regenerate this new analysis directory only. SIX_CLOSED_SOURCE_DATA.json preserves all original/new identity roles, RESULT/raw/exit SHA, exact options, cumulative additive fields and separate means/gauges/peaks. Both new CH strict/archive/native-restore audits are retained. ACTUAL_INPUT_AND_KERNEL_CONTRACT.json and BOUNDED_ACTUAL_TRACE_HEADER.json pin the actual one-kernel contract; LATENCY_MISSINGNESS.json preserves empty means and explicit extrema; typed records preserve CHcommon/DHOO separation.','',f"CPU_VALIDATION.json: {v['count']}checks PASS; six closed sources, two independent newCH archive audits, zero live points consumed and zero runtime actions. Root alone publishes this packet.",'',tab(['Source','RESULT path','RESULT SHA256','UUID','Raw gzip SHA256'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['RESULT_path'],by[c,p]['RESULT_sha256'],by[c,p]['uuid'],by[c,p]['raw_gzip_sha256']]for c,p in pairs]),'']
